---
import CollegeLayout from '../../../layouts/CollegeLayout.astro';
import SourceBox from '../../../components/colleges/SourceBox.astro';

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://convert.gudmud.site/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Guides', item: 'https://convert.gudmud.site/guides/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Check UGC Recognition', item: 'https://convert.gudmud.site/guides/how-to-check-if-university-is-ugc-recognised/' },
  ],
};

const articleJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'How to Check if a University is UGC Recognised: Verification Steps',
  datePublished: '2026-11-15T00:00:00+05:30',
  dateModified: '2026-11-15T00:00:00+05:30',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Gudmud Colleges Editorial Team',
    url: 'https://convert.gudmud.site',
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Gudmud Colleges',
    url: 'https://convert.gudmud.site',
  },
  description: 'Avoid unaccredited and fake institutions by checking the official University Grants Commission statutory register.',
};
---

<CollegeLayout
  title="How to Check UGC Recognition of Universities | Gudmud"
  description="Learn how to verify if a university is recognized by the UGC. Step-by-step guide to checking official recognition lists, Section 2(f), and 12(B) status."
  canonical="https://convert.gudmud.site/guides/how-to-check-if-university-is-ugc-recognised/"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd, articleJsonLd]}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-12">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:underline">Guides</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-gray-900 font-medium">UGC Recognition</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header Section -->
    <header class="mb-8 border-b border-gray-200 pb-6">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 border border-emerald-200 mb-3">
        <span>Degree Validity & Compliance</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>UGC Act 1956</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
        How to Check UGC Recognition of Universities
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
        Under Indian law, a university can only award valid degrees if established under a Central Act, Provincial Act, or State Act, and recognized under Section 2(f) and 12(B) of the UGC Act, 1956. Here is how to verify any institution before paying admission fees.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Content -->
    <article class="prose prose-indigo max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">1. Check the Official UGC University Lists</h2>
      <p>
        The University Grants Commission publishes continuously updated registries of legitimate universities categorized by legal status:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Central Universities:</strong> Established by an Act of Parliament (e.g., Delhi University, JNU, BHU).</li>
        <li><strong>State Public Universities:</strong> Established by state legislative assemblies.</li>
        <li><strong>State Private Universities:</strong> Established under state private university acts; cannot establish off-campus study centers outside their home state without UGC approval.</li>
        <li><strong>Deemed to be Universities:</strong> High-performing institutes granted university status under Section 3 of the UGC Act (e.g., BITS Pilani, IISc Bangalore).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">2. Step-by-Step UGC Portal Verification</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3">
        <li>
          Navigate to the official UGC portal at <a href="https://www.ugc.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-emerald-700 font-semibold underline">ugc.gov.in</a> (or use our direct <a href="/official-links/" class="text-emerald-700 font-semibold underline">official links directory</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Click on the <strong>Universities</strong> tab in the main navigation menu.
        </li>
        <li>
          Select the category matching the institute (e.g., <em>Private Universities</em> or <em>Deemed to be Universities</em>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Search for the state and locate the institute's exact name. Note the date of establishment and gazette notification reference.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">3. Checking the UGC "Fake Universities" List</h2>
      <p>
        UGC regularly publishes a statutory list of self-styled, unapproved institutions that operate without degree-granting authority. Degrees from these entities are legally invalid for government employment, higher education, or competitive exams.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-red-900 mb-1">Warning: Off-Campus & Franchise Center Traps</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-red-800 leading-relaxed">
          State Private Universities are prohibited from opening franchise centers, study centers, or off-campus centers outside their approved territorial jurisdiction. Enrolling in an unapproved distance learning branch may leave you with an invalid degree.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">4. Section 12(B) Status</h2>
      <p>
        Section 12(B) of the UGC Act declares an institution fit to receive central financial assistance from UGC. While non-12(B) private universities can still confer valid degrees if covered under 2(f), 12(B) status is an indicator of mature infrastructure, faculty strength, and research capacity.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Explore Recognized Public Institutions</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
          All 119 institutions featured on Gudmud Colleges are verified central institutes (IITs, NITs, IIITs, and Central Universities):
        </p>
        <a href="/colleges/" class="inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2 bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 text-white rounded-lg text-xs font-semibold shadow-sm">
          Browse 119 Verified Institutions →
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Source Box -->
    <div class="mt-12">
      <SourceBox
        sourceName="University Grants Commission (UGC)"
        sourceUrl="https://www.ugc.gov.in"
        sourceYear={2024}
        verifiedAt="2026-11-15"
        methodologyNote="Statutory verification procedures per University Grants Commission Act, 1956 and UGC (Establishment of and Maintenance of Standards in Private Universities) Regulations."
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</CollegeLayout>
